[agent] Confirmed: the failure is unconditional and independent of the metric argument. I've identified the exact defect. Per the probe instructions, this is a broken command in the interface under test, so I'll stop here and report it precisely rather than route around it with a job/SDK script (which would no longer measure the CLI).
[agent] ## Outcome: the CLI cannot create a vector-capable store — `hops fg create --embedding` is broken
[agent] **What works.** The CLI authenticates and connects fine (`hops context` reaches project `mlpab9089c4`, FS ID 3278). The relevant subcommands exist and are the right shape for this task:
[agent] - `hops fg create … --embedding "col:dim[:metric]"` — register a vector FG (auto-enables online).
[agent] - `hops fg insert` — load rows.
[agent] - `hops fg search --vector … --k 5` — "Run a KNN similarity search against a feature group's embedding column."
[agent] The platform/SDK fully supports this: `hsfs.embedding.SimilarityFunctionType.L2 = "l2_norm"` is exactly the Euclidean metric the task needs, and `EmbeddingIndex.add_embedding(name, dimension, similarity_function_type, model)` is a valid SDK call.
[agent] **The blocker.** `hops fg create --embedding` fails unconditionally before any backend call, with:
[agent] ```
[agent] TypeError: EmbeddingIndex.add_embedding() missing 1 required positional argument: 'dimension'
[agent] ```
[agent] The defect is in the CLI wrapper, `venv/.../hopsworks/cli/commands/fg.py`, function `_build_embedding` (lines 1076–1079). It parses `col:dim:metric` correctly but then calls the SDK wrong — it passes a constructed `EmbeddingFeature` object as the **first positional arg** (`name`), leaving the required `dimension` unfilled:
[agent] ```python
[agent] index.add_embedding(
[agent]     EmbeddingFeature(name=col, dimension=dim, similarity_function_type=metric)
[agent] )
[agent] ```
[agent] The SDK signature is `add_embedding(self, name, dimension, similarity_function_type=..., model=None)`. The correct call is:
[agent] ```python
[agent] index.add_embedding(name=col, dimension=dim, similarity_function_type=metric)
[agent] ```
[agent] I reproduced it both with a metric (`embedding:16:l2_norm`) and without (`embedding:16`) — same crash, so it's not input-dependent.
[agent] **Why this blocks the whole task.** Creating an embedding index is only reachable through `fg create --embedding`; there is no `fg add-embedding`/`append-embedding` subcommand to attach a vector index to an already-created FG, and `fg search` (KNN) requires that index to exist. So with this bug the CLI cannot create the store, cannot make it vector-searchable, and therefore cannot run the L2 KNN queries. I did not write `submission/answers.json`, because the only honest value would have to come from the platform's own vector search, which the CLI cannot stand up.
[agent] **Fix needed in the interface.** One-line change in `_build_embedding` to call `EmbeddingIndex.add_embedding(name=col, dimension=dim, similarity_function_type=metric)` instead of passing an `EmbeddingFeature` instance. After that fix, the intended CLI flow (`fg create --embedding "embedding:16:l2_norm"` → `fg insert --file data/items.csv` → `fg search --vector … --k 5` per query) should complete the task end-to-end.
